import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioFixNonLastOther
import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRulesAllSheet

/-!
# The patch `TrioFixNonLastOther` against the sheet, with every check of `TrioRulesAllSheet`

`TrioFixNonLastOther.lean` is `TrioRulesAll.lean` (rules 1–10 of
[koteitan/trio](https://github.com/koteitan/trio) with Fixes A–E and N) with Fix G
(Fix N outside the tower regimes), Fix M (marked levels that are not a top), no
storey for a spent ladder in an uncountable regime, and lifted leaves `b + n`.  This
file re-runs Parts 1–7 of `TrioRulesAllSheet.lean` for the patched rules
(`trioRuleMatrixOfAll`, `allOf`, `MAll`, `MstepAll`, `MfuelAll` replaced by
`trioRuleMatrixOfX`, `xOf`, `MX`, `MstepX`, `MfuelX`), then adds the patch's own
guards (Part 8).

* **The sheet**
  ([`tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv`](https://github.com/koteitan/trio/blob/main/tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv)):
  all 831 guards of Part 1 hold unchanged; the patch changes no matrix on the 822
  sheet labels, nor on Fix N's families `familyW` and `family1`.
* **The order checks**: the 783 chosen matrices and the 784 with the printed label of
  row 3552: 0 disagreements.
* **Parts 5–6.**  The patch changes 3 of the 71 nearby ordinals of Fix N
  (`Ω_{Ω_ω}+Ω_ω+1`, `Ω_{Ω_ω}+Ω_ω·2`, `Ω_{Ω_ω}+Ω_ω+Ω`; all three become standard, so
  15 → 12 are not standard, yaBMS `bms -s` outside Lean) and 3 of the 20 labels where
  Fix E and Fix N meet; the order counts stay (25 and 20 on the 71, 0 and 3 on the 20).
* **Part 7** (one step, same `Mf`): against rules 1–10 the counts by branch are
  `(countable 171 0) (psi 32 6) (omega 152 7) (sum 870 259)` (257 without the patch);
  against the merged step `MstepAll`, only 6 sums differ.
* **Part 8**: five families (688 labels after `Ω_{Ω_ω}`, `Ω_{Ω_{ω+1}}`, `Ω_{Ω_2}`,
  and with marked levels after `Ω_{Ω_Ω}` and `Ω_Ω`): order disagreements
  `1, 0, 0, 3, 1` (without the patch `3263, 2335, 1335, 928, 147`), colliding pairs
  `0, 0, 0, 2, 1` (`173, 174, 30, 91, 22`).  Not standard (yaBMS, outside Lean):
  `3, 0, 0, 3, 0` (`90, 17, 36, 0, 0`).  27 BMS expansions `M(P+t·ω)[n] = M(P+t·(n+1))`
  (`n = 1, 2`); without the patch `[2]` fails on all 27 and `[1]` on 9.  The lifted
  copies of change 4, and the pairs still out of order, by name.

All of it is `#guard`s: a calibration, not a theorem.
-/

