/-! ## Part 5: against rules 1–10 and the single-fix versions

`interactionsX ls` lists the labels of `ls` where the patched matrix is not the one
expected with no interaction: `TrioRulesNonLast`'s when Fix E changes nothing
(`TrioRules3` = `TrioRules2`), `TrioRules3`'s when Fix N changes nothing, and any
label that both fixes change.  A label that only this patch changes is listed too. -/

/-- The labels where Fix E and Fix N interact, or the patched matrix is unexpected. -/
def interactionsX (ls : List String) : List String :=
  ls.filter fun s =>
    let a := xOf s
    let o := ruleOf2 s
    let e := ruleOf3 s
    let n := nOf s
    (e == o && a != n) || (n == o && a != e) || (e != o && n != o)

